## PHASE 3: Rule Files Generation

**Generate rule files ONE AT A TIME. WRITE each file to the output directory, then show a SHORT summary in chat. User reviews the file in their IDE — NOT in chat.**

> **⚠️ PROGRESSIVE FILE WRITING (MANDATORY):**
> - **DO:** Write file → show 3-5 line summary + file path → ask user to review the file
> - **DON'T:** Dump entire file contents as a code block in chat
> - This follows the same pattern as the Technical Design Agent — content goes in files, not in conversation

> **Why per-file checkpoints?** Generating all 4-6 files in one pass causes Attention Drift (LLM Gap #1) and Error Cascade (LLM Gap #11). Each file builds on the previous — errors in Main Entry propagate to Phase Orchestration, then to Guidance and Stop Points. Per-file review catches issues early.

> **Reference agents** (study the one matching the selected archetype):
> - Document Generator → `examples/reference-agent-01-technical-design/` (full agent, all files)
> - Code Generator → `examples/reference-agent-03-app-development/` (Main Entry + README)
> - Analyzer → `examples/reference-agent-04-munit-testing/` (Main Entry + README)
> - Conversational → `examples/reference-agent-agent-tuner/` (Main Entry + README)
>
> **Architecture standard**: `lib/docs/AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_STANDARD.md`
> **Skeleton templates**: See `@01_Guidance.mdc` Section 2
> **Prompt techniques**: See `@01_Guidance.mdc` Section 3

**Output directory for drafts:** `project/output_builder/{agent-name}/`
Files are written here first, then moved to final location in Phase 7.

**Generation order (one file at a time — WRITE TO FILE, not chat):**

### 3A. Main Entry (`{ID}_{Agent}.mdc`)
- Frontmatter (description, author, version, alwaysApply: true, priority: HIGHEST)
- RISEN framework table (from Phase 2)
- Lean architecture table
- Phase workflow table
- Critical rules
- Mandatory behavior
- Output structure
- Quick reference

**Sub-checkpoint 3A:** WRITE file to `project/output_builder/{agent-name}/rules/{ID}_{Agent}.mdc`. Then show in chat:
```
✅ FILE WRITTEN: rules/{ID}_{Agent}.mdc (Main Entry)

📄 Contains: RISEN framework, {N}-phase workflow table, {N} critical rules, 
   {N} mandatory behaviors, output structure, quick reference
📏 Lines: ~{count} | Priority: HIGHEST | alwaysApply: true

👉 Please open and review the file, then reply:
→ "approved" to proceed to next file
→ Describe specific changes needed (I'll update the file)
```
STOP. Wait for approval before proceeding to 3B.

### 3B. Template Configuration (`{ID}-00_Template_Configuration.mdc`) — 5-file agents only
- Template location
- Pre-generation checklist
- Template structure
- Template-driven rules

**Sub-checkpoint 3B:** WRITE file to output directory. Show short summary + file path in chat. STOP. Wait for approval before proceeding to 3C. (Skip for 4-file agents.)

### 3C. Phase Orchestration (`0X_Phase_Orchestration.mdc`)
- State machine diagram (Mermaid `stateDiagram-v2`) — **MUST follow `@lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md` §2 (ten rules), §5 (layout control via declaration order), §12 (state diagram specifics), §14 (pre-emit self-check)**. States declared in phase order; `[*]` for start/end; transitions labeled with trigger events (`user approved`), not actions.
- Phase specifications (per phase from Phase 2)
- `<thinking>` block template
- Confidence Calibration table
- RGV pattern per generation phase
- State file JSON schema
- Error recovery table
- Quick reference
- **If `progressiveDocV2: true` (DEFAULT for multi-phase analytical agents):**
  - PROGRESSIVE DOCUMENTATION v2 — PER-PHASE WRITE CONTRACT section (table mapping Phase → Section(s) Written → Marker(s) → Mode). See `@01_Guidance.mdc` §10.4 for the embeddable template.
  - Phase 0 task list MUST include "Create deliverable skeleton with named placeholders" as Step 1.
  - Every generation phase MUST include an explicit `**Artifact Writes (Phase N — Progressive Documentation v2):**` task block citing the section marker(s) it writes to.
  - The final-output phase MUST be reframed as "Consolidate & Polish" (not "Generate Final {document}") with explicit CONSOLIDATE-mode task list (re-read file, cross-section consistency edits, terminology alignment, residual-placeholder check, final style/length self-check against `exampleAnchorPath`).
  - See `lib/docs/prompt-engineering-patterns.md` Pattern #20 v2 for the canonical block to embed.

**Sub-checkpoint 3C:** WRITE file to output directory. Show short summary + file path in chat. STOP. Wait for approval before proceeding to 3D.

### 3D. Guidance (`0X_Guidance.mdc`)
- Domain-specific patterns
- Few-shot examples (bad→good) for the agent's domain
- Decision matrices (if applicable)
- Quality checklist — **MUST include an Example-Anchored Conciseness item if `progressiveDocV2: true`**: "Output verbosity benchmarked against `{exampleAnchorPath}`; structural budgets (sentence counts per executive section, table density, K-word quote rule) preferred over hard line caps." See `@01_Guidance.mdc` §10.5.
- **Mermaid Diagram Standards section** — embed the template from `@01_Guidance.mdc` §12.2, adapted to the agent's domain. Reference either the Agent Builder canonical at `@r-genie/Agent_Builder/lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md` OR copy the doc into the agent's own `lib/docs/` and reference locally. This is MANDATORY for any agent whose output includes Mermaid diagrams.
- **Progressive Documentation v2 Section (if `progressiveDocV2: true`)** — embed an adapted version of `@01_Guidance.mdc` §10 (Five Mechanics + Skeleton Convention + Per-Phase Write Contract Template + Example-Anchored Conciseness) into the generated agent's Guidance file. Adapt the section markers, file names, and phase-to-section mapping to the agent's domain.
- Quick reference

