## PHASE 6: Validation

**Two-tier validation: structural compliance + semantic quality.**

### 6A. Structural Validation (against `AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_STANDARD.md`)

| Check | What |
|-------|------|
| RISEN Complete | All 5 elements defined |
| Dual-Author Attribution | All files have R-GENIE framework footer + agent author footer |
| Quick Reference | Every rule file has table |
| File Size | Main ≤200, Phase ≤400, Guidance ≤600, Stops ≤450 |
| Cross-References | All `@file.mdc` valid |
| Version Consistency | All files same version |
| Frontmatter | All .mdc files have required fields |
| Prompt Techniques | All 14 techniques present |
| Rules/Templates Decoupling | No section numbers in rules (5-file agents) |
| Mermaid Diagram Standards | Every `flowchart`/`graph` block has `%%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%` directive; zero `\n` in labels; styles at end in node-declaration order; runs the §14 self-check in `@lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md`. Applies to ALL emitted diagrams: Phase Orchestration state machine, INDEX.md Rule Dependency Map + Phase Workflow, ARCHITECTURE.md flow diagram, and any domain deliverable diagrams. |
| Progressive Documentation v2 Embedding (if `progressiveDocV2: true`) | Generated Phase Orchestration contains PER-PHASE WRITE CONTRACT section (Phase → Section table); every generation phase has `**Artifact Writes (Phase N):**` block; final phase is reframed as Consolidate & Polish; Phase 0 task list includes "Create deliverable skeleton with named placeholders" as Step 1; Stop Points file contains PER-PHASE WRITE SELF-CHECK block; Guidance file contains adapted §10 (Five Mechanics + Example-Anchored Conciseness). See `@01_Guidance.mdc` §10 and `lib/docs/prompt-engineering-patterns.md` Pattern #20 v2. |

### 6B. Semantic Validation (substance, not just format)

| Check | What | Fail Condition |
|-------|------|----------------|
| RISEN Specificity | Each RISEN element uses domain-specific language | Generic phrases like "Expert who helps users" or "User provides stuff" |
| Phase Distinctness | Each phase has a unique purpose and deliverable | Two phases with overlapping tasks or identical deliverables |
| Few-Shot Relevance | BAD/GOOD examples reference the stated domain | Generic examples unrelated to user's goal from Phase 0 |
| Stop Point Decision-Value | Each stop justifies why user judgment matters | Stops at trivial/mechanical steps where no human decision is needed |
| Domain Keyword Presence | Generated rules contain domain-specific terminology from Phase 0 | Rule files could apply to any domain (no domain fingerprint) |
| Cross-File Coherence | RISEN in Main Entry matches phase tasks in Orchestration | Main Entry says "5-phase" but Orchestration defines 7 phases |
| Constitutional Principle #4 | 4th principle is domain-adapted, not generic | Uses default "COMPLETENESS over brevity" without considering the domain |

### 6C. Ecosystem Validation (if inside `r-genie/`)

| Check | What |
|-------|------|
| Folder Name Uniqueness | `{Name}_Agent/` folder doesn't collide with existing agents in `AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_STANDARD.md` §12 (e.g., `Cloud_Success_Architect_Agent/` is fine if no existing folder matches) |
| Output Path Uniqueness | `project/output_{agent-slug}/` path doesn't overlap with existing agents (e.g., `project/output_cloud_success_architect/`) |
| Activation File Names | `use-{agent-slug}.md` in `.windsurf/workflows/` and `.cursor/commands/` has no naming conflict with existing files |
| No Numeric Prefix | Generated folder is NOT prefixed with a numeric sequence (`11_`, `12_`, etc.) — this is a Phase 1 guardrail; legacy `XX_` prefixes are frozen on agents 00–08 only |

**Checkpoint:** STOP. Show validation report (structural + semantic results). Flag any semantic failures for user decision: fix or accept.

